 sporting goods, jewelry, toys, household items, and apparel. The company offers its deal offerings to customers through websites; search engines; applications and mobile websites, which enable consumers to browse, purchase, manage, and redeem deals on their mobile devices; emails and push notifications; affiliate channels; social and display advertising; and offline marketing. Groupon, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dusan  Senkypl | CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $214,212 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $287K ranks in the bottom quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 51%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Groupon, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $496M market cap on $498M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and -17% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 562% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 554-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 56% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $50M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-2.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (49.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 411% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.114205839718369},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 56/100): structural revenue/margin decline; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Communication Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 65% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Communication Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here is What to Know Beyond Why Groupon, Inc. (GRPN) is a Trending Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029341/here-is-what-to-know-beyond-why-groupon-inc-grpn-is-a-trending-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3029341","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794574805.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Groupon Inc (GRPN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Billings Rise 6% but Revenue and EBITDA ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/groupon-inc-grpn-q3-2026-010456953.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794359096.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Groupon (GRPN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/groupon-grpn-q3-2026-earnings-191355000.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794338480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Investors Got Wrong About Groupon Before The Drop","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/investors-got-wrong-groupon-drop-081134838.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471094.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Groupon: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/groupon-3-key-takeaways-long-043202186.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794371522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ajay V. Mittal Awarded 7,036 RSUs Following Groupon Board Appointment","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/ajay-v-mittal-awarded-7036-rsus-following-groupon-board-appointment","date":"2026-11-11",